# More info: https://docs.docker.com/engine/reference/builder/#dockerignore-file
#
# Ignore everything by default and re-include only what a build needs. That
# direction is the right one — a deny-by-default context cannot accidentally
# ship a .env or a 400 MB model file — but it has one sharp edge, and this
# project has already been cut by it.
#
# ANY FILE A BINARY EMBEDS MUST BE RE-INCLUDED HERE.
#
# `//go:embed` is resolved by the COMPILER, not at runtime, and a pattern that
# matches nothing is a compile ERROR:
#
#     internal/observability/dashboards.go:48:12:
#         pattern dashboards/*.json: no matching files found
#
# So a missing re-include does not degrade the image, it fails the build — but
# only inside the container. `go build` on a developer's machine sees the files
# and succeeds, so the breakage is invisible until CI builds an image. That is
# exactly how the Grafana dashboards got here: added in Sprint 3, never built
# into an image until Sprint 7's CI run.
#
# TestEmbeddedFilesSurviveTheDockerContext enforces this automatically.
**

# Re-include Go source files (but not *_test.go)
!**/*.go
**/*_test.go

# Re-include Go module files
!go.mod
!go.sum

# Re-include embedded assets. See the note above: these are compile-time
# dependencies of internal/observability, not optional extras.
!internal/observability/dashboards/*.json
